Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 15:46:29 +0200
Subject: QTest::CrashHandler: Use accessor to read the program counter on
 arm64

We were reading the program counter directly from the __pc field of
the Darwin ARM thread state. That field only exists on plain arm64.

On arm64e, pointer authentication is enabled, and the SDK makes the
thread state fields opaque (__pc becomes __opaque_pc), since the values
are signed pointers that must be authenticated before use. Accessing
__pc directly then fails to compile.

We now go through the arm_thread_state64_get_pc() accessor macro, which
handles the PAC bits on arm64e and just returns the raw field on plain
arm64, so it works for both.

Fixes: QTBUG-147612
Pick-to: 6.12 6.11
Change-Id: Icf46a7ae658b03e601322dac156e01349d43e2d9
Reviewed-by: Thiago Macieira <thiago.macieira@intel.com>
(cherry picked from commit 7b484f99cff76c13e1cad4ab44b8dcbda5bd07da)
---
 src/testlib/qtestcrashhandler_unix.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git x/qtbase/src/testlib/qtestcrashhandler_unix.cpp y/qtbase/src/testlib/qtestcrashhandler_unix.cpp
index e6b845b84b3f9298fc31b687451a3bbdec3feda3..3f5a4f0e87312229939736128f16c27ebc3222b0 100644
--- x/qtbase/src/testlib/qtestcrashhandler_unix.cpp
+++ y/qtbase/src/testlib/qtestcrashhandler_unix.cpp
@@ -372,7 +372,7 @@ static quintptr getProgramCounter(void *ucontext)
 #if 0 // keep the list below alphabetical
 
 #elif defined(Q_OS_DARWIN) && defined(Q_PROCESSOR_ARM_64)
-        pc = ctx->uc_mcontext->__ss.__pc;
+        pc = arm_thread_state64_get_pc(ctx->uc_mcontext->__ss);
 #elif defined(Q_OS_DARWIN) && defined(Q_PROCESSOR_X86_64)
         pc = ctx->uc_mcontext->__ss.__rip;
 
